WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.822
On this slide, we are focusing on add a docstring.

00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:08.657
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:14.642
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.642 --> 00:00:18.322
A docstring explains what a function is designed to do.

00:00:18.322 --> 00:00:24.117
Good documentation makes the expected inputs and returned result easier to understand.

00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:27.252
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:33.402
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:33.402 --> 00:00:36.742
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:36.742 --> 00:00:41.759
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
